The reflected power ratio of a transmission line can be determined as:

$$V_{r}/V_{i} = (Z_{L} - Z_{0})/(Z_{L} + Z_{0})$$

Where $$Z_{L}$$ is the load impedance and $$Z_{0}$$ is the characteristic impedance of the transmission line.

At 50 ohms, the reflected power is determined as:

$$|V_{r}/V_{i}|^{2} = (75 - 50)/(75 + 50) = 0.2$$

Which implies 20 % of the power is reflected.

If the load is reduced to 50 ohms, the reflected power will become:

$$|V_{r}/V_{i}|^{2} = (50 - 50)/(50 + 50) = 0.01$$

Which implies only 1 % of the power is reflected.
